#[doc("""
Native build entry points: owned text, core objects and separate compilation.

What the partition that owns a program's singletons emits beyond the
functions it defines, as text for its cache key: the default handlers
it installs and the globals it defines for them, the impl table it
registers, and the runner driver.

Each part is read from the value its emitter walks, so the key moves
whenever the object would. A singleton the owner gains belongs here in
the same change, or two builds that differ only in it share one object.

compiler/emit_native_core.kai — the whole-program native build split into a
cached CORE object plus a per-build USER object.

Every fn homing to an auto-loaded core module (plus the lambdas those fns
lift, whose symbols embed their enclosing module) emits into ONE core
object, content-addressed under the shared core cache dir. The core's KIR
is a pure function of the core sources — monomorphised instances of core
generics home to the root, so a user program cannot perturb the partition —
and the key folds everything else that shapes the object (toolchain id,
edition, target triple, opt level, runtime-bitcode ids, core source
hashes). A warm build therefore links the stored object and only lowers,
optimises and emits the user's own partition.

Soundness is the modular-cache model: a stale object cannot be linked
because the key IS the content — any drift in what would be emitted (or in
what emits it) produces a different filename, and a miss re-emits. Both
partitions are raw (external-linkage) emissions of the SAME whole-program
tables, so their ABIs agree by construction, exactly like native-modular
partitions.

compiler/emit_native_modular.kai — the native separate-compilation driver.

The frontend stays whole-program: parse / infer / perceus / monomorph run
once and produce ONE `KProgram`. This backend partitions only the CODEGEN —
it projects that whole-program `KProgram` onto one LLVM module per `KFn.mo`
(the `home_tu` partition L2 stamped) plus the root, emits each to its own
object, and returns the object paths for the driver to link. The per-module
object is a PROJECTION of the whole-program computation, never an isolated
compile: every partition declares the SAME whole-program fn table, so their
ABIs agree by construction and no serialised signature can drift.

What lands where (asu-reviewed):
  root TU  — every fn with `mo = None` (private fns, lambdas, clauses, the
             user `main`), the proto impl-table init, the
             default install/teardown, the default-evidence global DEFINITIONS
             (external), and the synthetic `kai_main` runner driver. It is the
             runtime owner, so the runtime links against it.
  leaf TU  — every fn homing to that module; the default globals and the other
             modules' fns it calls are EXTERNAL declarations resolved at link.
  Every TU carries the thunk of each fn it defines, so a closure over a fn
  of another module resolves the definition that module's object holds.

Cache: each partition's object is content-addressed on the hash of its
projected KIR — the fns it DEFINES plus every program fn's SIGNATURE (so a
producer's signature/ownership flip rewrites a consumer's key). With a cache
dir, a hit reuses the stored object and SKIPS codegen; only changed partitions
re-emit. Without one, every partition emits to `<out_dir>/<stem>.o`.
""")]

import compiler.ast_decl
import compiler.ast_ids
import compiler.emit_native
import compiler.emit_native_def
import compiler.emit_native_fn
import compiler.emit_native_proto
import compiler.emit_shared_proto
import compiler.emit_shared_syms
import compiler.enc_unit
import compiler.fn_index
import compiler.fnreg
import compiler.infer_index
import compiler.kir
import compiler.kir_syms
import compiler.ncore_index
import compiler.spec_names
import compiler.symtab
import compiler.user_cache
import compiler.util

#[doc("The text of what the owner of the singletons of `kp` emits for them in a `bmode` build.")]
fn nowned_text(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn], bmode: BuildMode) : String =
  concat_all([
    "entry defaults\n", nowned_defaults_text(kp.tab, nemit_entry_defaults(kp, bmode)),
    "default globals\n", nowned_defaults_text(kp.tab, kp.synth_defaults),
    nproto_init_text(decls, kp.tab, kp.ids, variants, fns, kp.reuse_tags),
    "runners ", nowned_mode_word(bmode), "\n", concat_all(map(kp.runners, nowned_runner_text))
  ])

fn nowned_defaults_text(tab: SymTab, ds: [KDefault]) : String = concat_all(map(ds, (d) => match d {
  KDef(eff, ops) -> concat_all([rt_name(tab, eff), ":", concat_all(map(ops, nowned_op_text)), "\n"])
}))

fn nowned_op_text(op: KDefOp) : String = match op {
  KDOp(name, sym, arity) -> concat_all([" ", name, "=", sym, "/", int_to_string(arity)])
}

fn nowned_mode_word(bmode: BuildMode) : String = match bmode {
  BMBuild -> "build"
  BMTest  -> "test"
  BMBench -> "bench"
  BMCheck -> "check"
}

fn nowned_runner_text(r: KRunner) : String =
  concat_all([r.sym, " ", int_to_string(r.line), " ", r.home, " ", nowned_kind_text(r.kind), " ", r.desc, "\n"])

fn nowned_kind_text(k: KRunnerKind) : String = match k {
  KRTest         -> "test"
  KRBench        -> "bench"
  KRCheck(specs) -> cat2("check ", string_join(specs, ";"))
}

#[doc("Configuration of the native core-object cache: the writable cache dir, the toolchain id, the edition, the backend tag (triple, opt level, bitcode ids), the joined core source hashes, the stats toggle, and the pre-key the obtained object is recorded under (empty records nothing).")]
pub type NCoreCfg = { dir: String, toolchain: String, edition: String,
                      tag: String, srcs_hex: String, stats: Bool, pre: String }

#[doc("Emit the program as a user object at `obj_path` plus a content-addressed core object under the cache dir, reusing the stored core object on a key hit. Returns the object paths to link (user first), or empty on a codegen failure. Falls back to the single whole-program object when the core partition is empty, the backend tag is empty, or the core emit fails.")]
pub fn build_native_core_split(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry],
                               fns: [EFn], bmode: BuildMode, obj_path: String,
                               src_path: String, cfg: NCoreCfg,
                               core_names: [String]) : [String] / Console + File = {
  let emit_fns = kp.fns
  let stems = ncore_stems(core_names)
  let nm = kp_names(kp)
  let core_fns = ncore_core_fns(nm, emit_fns, stems)
  if list_length(core_fns) == 0 {
    ncore_whole(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, obj_path, src_path)
  } else if cfg.tag == "" {
    # An empty tag means the key would not fold the toolchain/bitcode state:
    # objects built under different runtime models would collide on one key
    # and a warm hit could hand the link an object whose extern expectations
    # the runtime TU does not meet. Never cache in that state.
    let _w = eprint("kaic2: warning: native core-object cache disengaged: empty backend tag reached the split")
    ncore_whole(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, obj_path, src_path)
  } else {
    # A failed core emit degrades to the whole-program object, where a
    # codegen failure re-surfaces its diagnostics.
    let env = ndecl_env(kp, decls)
    match ncore_obtain(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, core_fns, cfg, obj_path, env) {
      None -> ncore_whole(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, obj_path, src_path)
      Some(co) -> ncore_emit_user(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path,
                                  ncore_user_fns(nm, emit_fns, stems), obj_path, co, env)
    }
  }
}

#[doc("Emit only the user partition and link it against `core_obj`, a core object the cache already holds. For a program whose core was pruned before typing: the user partition is the same as in a full build, since core generics instantiate into the root.")]
pub fn build_native_core_reuse(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
    bmode: BuildMode, obj_path: String, src_path: String, core_obj: String, core_names: [String],
    stats: Bool) : [String] / Console = {
  ncore_note(stats, "kaic2: native-core-obj: hit (core pruned)")
  let user = ncore_user_fns(kp_names(kp), kp.fns, ncore_stems(core_names))
  ncore_emit_user(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, user, obj_path, core_obj, ndecl_env(kp, decls))
}

#[doc("The program without the fns nothing can reach: roots are the core partition, the root module's own fns, every FFI wrapper, every protocol impl the startup table registers, and in a test or bench build the runner bodies. Keeping the core whole keeps the cached core object program-invariant.")]
pub fn ncore_prune_unreachable(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], fns: [EFn], bmode: BuildMode,
                               core_names: [String]) : KProgram = {
  let stems = ncore_stems(core_names)
  let runners = ncore_runner_syms(kp.runners)
  let live_runners = if nemit_is_runner_mode(bmode) { runners } else { [] }
  let fx = fnx_build(fns)
  let nm = kp_names(kp)
  let root = sym_owner(kp.tab, kp.entry)
  kir_reachable(kp, (f) => ncore_is_core(nm, f, stems) or ncore_is_own(nm, f, root),
                list_append(ncore_pimpl_syms(fx, collect_pimpl_rows(decls, fx, kp.ids, [])), live_runners))
}

# A root-module fn the user wrote (not a lambda, clause, mono instance or
# runner body, which are reached through their referrers), or an FFI wrapper
# from any module.
fn ncore_is_own(nm: KNames, f: KFn, root: SymId) : Bool = match f.kind {
  KFnFfi(_, _, _) -> true
  KFnNormal -> match f.mo {
    None    -> ncore_is_decl(f.unit) and not (ncore_unit_is_mono(f.unit))
    Some(m) -> sym_same(st_module_id(m), root) and ncore_is_decl(f.unit) and not (ncore_unit_is_mono(f.unit))
  }
  _ -> false
}

fn ncore_is_decl(u: EncUnit) : Bool = match u {
  EuFn(_) -> true
  _       -> false
}

fn ncore_pimpl_syms(fx: FnIndex, rows: [PimplRow]) : [String] = map(rows, (pr) => pimpl_csym(fx, pr))

fn ncore_runner_syms(rs: [KRunner]) : [String] = match rs {
  [] -> []
  [r, ...rest] -> [r.sym, ...ncore_runner_syms(rest)]
}

# Empty core partition: the plain whole-program object, single path.
fn ncore_whole(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
               bmode: BuildMode, obj_path: String, src_path: String) : [String] / Console =
  if build_native_object(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, obj_path, src_path) == 0 {
    [obj_path]
  } else { [] }

# The core object to link: the cached one on a key hit, a freshly emitted one
# on a miss, `None` on a codegen failure. A cache that cannot be written
# gets nothing: the object is emitted beside the user object instead, so a
# build never depends on being able to write its cache.
fn ncore_obtain(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
                bmode: BuildMode, src_path: String, core_fns: [KFn],
                cfg: NCoreCfg, obj_path: String, env: NDeclEnv) : Option[String] / Console + File = {
  let core_obj = concat_all([cfg.dir, "/ncore-", ncore_key(kp, core_fns, cfg), ".o"])
  let hit = match __file_read(core_obj) { Ok(_) -> true Err(_) -> false }
  let kept = hit or ncore_writes(core_obj)
  let _s = if cfg.stats {
    eprint(cat2("kaic2: native-core-obj: ", if hit { "hit" } else if kept { "miss" } else { "miss, cache not writable" }))
  } else { () }
  let dest = if kept { core_obj } else { cat2(obj_path, ".core.o") }
  if hit { ncore_recorded(cfg, core_obj) }
  else if not ncore_emit(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, core_fns, NModSplitCore, "kai_native_core", dest, env) { None }
  else if kept { ncore_recorded(cfg, core_obj) }
  else { Some(dest) }
}

# Whether the cache takes a new object.
fn ncore_writes(core_obj: String) : Bool / File = {
  let probe = cat2(core_obj, ".probe")
  match __file_write(probe, "") {
    Ok(_)  -> { let _d = __file_delete(probe); true }
    Err(_) -> false
  }
}

fn ncore_recorded(cfg: NCoreCfg, core_obj: String) : Option[String] / Console + File = {
  ncore_index_record(cfg.dir, cfg.pre, core_obj, cfg.stats)
  Some(core_obj)
}

fn ncore_note(stats: Bool, line: String) : Unit / Console = if stats { eprint(line) } else { () }

# Emit the user partition and return the pair to link (user first).
fn ncore_emit_user(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
                   bmode: BuildMode, src_path: String, user_fns: [KFn],
                   obj_path: String, core_obj: String, env: NDeclEnv) : [String] / Console =
  if ncore_emit(kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, user_fns, NModSplitRoot, "kai_native", obj_path, env) {
    [obj_path, core_obj]
  } else { [] }

# Build one partition module and emit it raw (external linkage, the
# separate-compilation runtime-bc merge). True on success. The core object's
# path is content-addressed, so a concurrent build racing on the same key
# writes byte-identical bytes.
fn ncore_emit(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
              bmode: BuildMode, src_path: String, define_fns: [KFn],
              role: NModRole, mod_name: String, obj: String, env: NDeclEnv) : Bool / Console = {
  let m = llvm_module_new(mod_name)
  let ctx = native_ctx_new(m)
  nemit_build_module(ctx, kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path,
                     define_fns, kp.fns, role, env)
  if native_ctx_ok(ctx) == 1 { llvm_emit_object_raw(m, obj) == 0 }
  else {
    eprint("native: core-split partition not emitted — a KIR node is outside the current subset (see above)")
    false
  }
}

# ---- partition ---------------------------------------------------------

# Core-module stems as they appear in mangled symbols (dots → underscores).
fn ncore_stems(core_names: [String]) : [String] = ncore_stems_loop(core_names, [])
fn ncore_stems_loop(ms: [String], acc: [String]) : [String] = match ms {
  [] -> list_reverse(acc)
  [m, ...rest] -> ncore_stems_loop(rest, [ncore_dots(m, 0, string_length(m), ""), ...acc])
}

fn ncore_dots(s: String, i: Int, n: Int, acc: String) : String =
  if i >= n { acc }
  else {
    let c = string_slice(s, i, 1)
    ncore_dots(s, i + 1, n, cat2(acc, if c == "." { "_" } else { c }))
  }

fn ncore_core_fns(nm: KNames, fns: [KFn], stems: [String]) : [KFn] =
  filter(fns, (f) => ncore_is_core(nm, f, stems))

fn ncore_user_fns(nm: KNames, fns: [KFn], stems: [String]) : [KFn] =
  filter(fns, (f) => not (ncore_is_core(nm, f, stems)))

# A fn belongs to the core partition when it homes to a core module, or when
# it is a lambda lifted from a core fn — a lambda's `mo` is None, but its
# symbol (`_kaiu_lam_<enc_fn>_<line>_<col>`) embeds the enclosing fn's
# module-mangled name, which is derived from the core source alone.
#
# Monomorphised instances are EXCLUDED even when they home to a core module:
# which instances exist depends on the program's call sites, so keeping them
# in the partition would fork the core key per program. They ride the user
# object instead (the baseline core carries essentially none, so the user
# partition stays small and the core object is program-invariant).
fn ncore_is_core(nm: KNames, f: KFn, stems: [String]) : Bool =
  if ncore_unit_is_mono(f.unit) { false }
  else { match f.mo {
    Some(m) -> list_has(stems, ncore_dots(m, 0, string_length(m), ""))
    None -> match f.kind {
      KFnLambda -> ncore_unit_is_core(nm, f.unit, stems)
      _         -> false
    }
  } }

# A unit is a specialisation's when the function it is, or is lifted out of,
# is an instance rather than the declaration itself.
fn ncore_unit_is_mono(u: EncUnit) : Bool = match u {
  EuFn(fid)            -> fnid_inst(fid) != spec_none()
  EuLam(o, _, _)       -> ncore_unit_is_mono(o)
  EuClause(o, _, _, _) -> ncore_unit_is_mono(o)
  EuFinally(o, _, _)   -> ncore_unit_is_mono(o)
  _                    -> false
}

# A lifted body is core when the declaration it is lifted out of is: a
# specialisation of a core fn is the program's, and so is what it holds.
fn ncore_unit_is_core(nm: KNames, u: EncUnit, stems: [String]) : Bool = match u {
  EuFn(fid)           -> fnid_inst(fid) == spec_none() and ncore_decl_is_core(idx_chain_sym(nm.reg, fnid_sym(fid)), fid, stems)
  EuLam(o, _, _)      -> ncore_unit_is_core(nm, o, stems)
  EuClause(o, _, _, _) -> ncore_unit_is_core(nm, o, stems)
  EuFinally(o, _, _)  -> ncore_unit_is_core(nm, o, stems)
  _                   -> false
}

fn ncore_decl_is_core(chain: [EFn], fid: FnId, stems: [String]) : Bool = match chain {
  []           -> false
  [e, ...rest] -> match e {
    EFn(_, _, mo, _, id) -> if fnid_eq(id, fid) {
      match mo {
        Some(m) -> list_has(stems, ncore_dots(m, 0, string_length(m), ""))
        None    -> false
      }
    } else { ncore_decl_is_core(rest, fid, stems) }
  }
}

# ---- content key -------------------------------------------------------

# The cached core object's key: the projected KIR (fns defined + referenced
# signatures, the modular-cache discipline) plus every out-of-KIR input that
# shapes the emitted object — toolchain id, edition, backend tag (triple, opt
# level, runtime-bitcode ids), and the core source hashes (evidence frames
# and effect rows derive from the sources without necessarily showing in the
# KIR dump). Any drift in any component misses; a hit is exact.
fn ncore_key(kp: KProgram, core_fns: [KFn], cfg: NCoreCfg) : String =
  uc_content_hex(concat_all([
    "NCO1\n", cfg.toolchain, "\n", cfg.edition, "\n", cfg.tag, "\n", cfg.srcs_hex, "\n",
    nmodkey_core(kp, core_fns)]))

#[doc("Emit the program as N native objects (root plus one per KFn.mo) and return their object paths, empty on a codegen failure. A Some cache_dir content-addresses each object and skips codegen on a hit. The caller links every returned path with the runtime owner.")]
pub fn build_native_modular(kp: KProgram, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry],
                            fns: [EFn], bmode: BuildMode, out_dir: String,
                            cache_dir: Option[String], src_path: String)
                            : [String] / Console + File = {
  let emit_fns = kp.fns
  let mods = nmod_distinct_modules(emit_fns, [])
  # One key context for the build: every partition is keyed on, and emitted
  # from, the same declaration analyses.
  let kc = nmodkey_ctx(kp, ndecl_env(kp, decls))
  let root = nmod_emit_one(kc, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, out_dir, cache_dir,
                           "__root__", nmod_fns_of(emit_fns, None), NModRoot)
  match root {
    None    -> []
    Some(r) -> nmod_emit_leaves(kc, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, out_dir,
                                cache_dir, emit_fns, mods, [r])
  }
}

# The distinct `Some(m)` module origins across the fn list, first-seen order.
fn nmod_distinct_modules(fns: [KFn], acc: [String]) : [String] = match fns {
  [] -> list_reverse(acc)
  [f, ...rest] -> match f.mo {
    None    -> nmod_distinct_modules(rest, acc)
    Some(m) -> if list_has(acc, m) { nmod_distinct_modules(rest, acc) }
               else                { nmod_distinct_modules(rest, [m, ...acc]) }
  }
}

# The fns homing to `mo` (`None` = root), preserving program order.
fn nmod_fns_of(fns: [KFn], mo: Option[String]) : [KFn] = nmod_fns_of_loop(fns, mo, [])
fn nmod_fns_of_loop(fns: [KFn], mo: Option[String], acc: [KFn]) : [KFn] = match fns {
  [] -> list_reverse(acc)
  [f, ...rest] -> if nmod_mo_eq(f.mo, mo) { nmod_fns_of_loop(rest, mo, [f, ...acc]) }
                  else                    { nmod_fns_of_loop(rest, mo, acc) }
}

fn nmod_mo_eq(a: Option[String], b: Option[String]) : Bool = match a {
  None    -> match b { None -> true  Some(_) -> false }
  Some(x) -> match b { None -> false Some(y) -> x == y }
}

# Emit each leaf module, threading the accumulated object-path list. A partition
# that fails codegen aborts the whole build (returns []), since a missing object
# would break the link.
fn nmod_emit_leaves(kc: NKeyCtx, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
                    bmode: BuildMode, src_path: String, out_dir: String,
                    cache_dir: Option[String], all_fns: [KFn], mods: [String],
                    acc: [String]) : [String] / Console + File = match mods {
  [] -> list_reverse(acc)
  [m, ...rest] -> {
    let a = nmod_emit_one(kc, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, out_dir, cache_dir,
                          nmod_stem(m), nmod_fns_of(all_fns, Some(m)), NModLeaf)
    match a {
      None    -> []
      Some(x) -> nmod_emit_leaves(kc, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, out_dir,
                                  cache_dir, all_fns, rest, [x, ...acc])
    }
  }
}

# Build one partition. On a cache hit (the content-addressed object already
# exists) codegen is skipped and the cached path returned; otherwise the module
# is built and emitted. Returns the object path, or `None` on a codegen failure.
fn nmod_emit_one(kc: NKeyCtx, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
                 bmode: BuildMode, src_path: String, out_dir: String,
                 cache_dir: Option[String], stem: String, define_fns: [KFn],
                 role: NModRole) : Option[String] / Console + File = {
  let key = nmod_cache_key(kc, decls, variants, fns, bmode, define_fns, role)
  let obj = nmod_obj_path(out_dir, cache_dir, stem, key)
  if nmod_cached(cache_dir, obj) { Some(obj) }
  else { nmod_build(kc, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, stem, define_fns, role, obj) }
}

# The object path: content-addressed `<cache_dir>/<key>.o` when a cache dir is
# set (so identical KIR reuses one object across builds), else `<out_dir>/<stem>.o`.
fn nmod_obj_path(out_dir: String, cache_dir: Option[String], stem: String, key: String) : String =
  match cache_dir {
    Some(d) -> concat_all([d, "/", key, ".o"])
    None    -> concat_all([out_dir, "/", stem, ".o"])
  }

# A cache hit iff a cache dir is set and the content-addressed object already
# exists — probed with `__file_read` (its `Ok` means present) rather than a
# dedicated exists prim, so kaic1 (which lacks that prim) still bootstraps.
fn nmod_cached(cache_dir: Option[String], obj: String) : Bool / File = match cache_dir {
  None    -> false
  Some(_) -> match __file_read(obj) { Ok(_) -> true Err(_) -> false }
}

# Build the LLVM module for this partition and emit its object with the raw
# (no runtime-bitcode-merge, no internalise) emitter so cross-TU symbols keep
# external linkage. A hit is probed by existence, so the emitter publishes the
# object atomically and a concurrent build never sees it half-written.
fn nmod_build(kc: NKeyCtx, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
              bmode: BuildMode, src_path: String, stem: String,
              define_fns: [KFn], role: NModRole, obj: String) : Option[String] / Console + File = {
  let m = llvm_module_new(cat2("kai_native_", stem))
  let ctx = native_ctx_new(m)
  nemit_build_module(ctx, kc.kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode, src_path, define_fns, kc.kp.fns, role, kc.env)
  if native_ctx_ok(ctx) == 1 {
    if llvm_emit_object_raw(m, obj) != 0 { None } else { Some(obj) }
  } else {
    eprint(concat_all(["native-modular: partition ", stem, " not emitted — a KIR node is outside the current subset (see above)"]))
    None
  }
}

# The partition's content-addressed cache key (see emit_native_modkey). The
# owner of the singletons emits them too, so its key folds their text; a
# leaf's stays free of the build mode.
fn nmod_cache_key(kc: NKeyCtx, decls: [Decl], variants: [VariantEntry], fns: [EFn],
                  bmode: BuildMode, define_fns: [KFn], role: NModRole) : String =
  nmodkey_of(kc, define_fns, nmod_role_tag(role),
             if nmod_owns_singletons(role) { nowned_text(kc.kp, decls, variants, fns, bmode) } else { "" })

fn nmod_role_tag(role: NModRole) : String = match role {
  NModWhole -> "whole"  NModRoot -> "root"  NModLeaf -> "leaf"
  NModSplitRoot -> "splitroot"  NModSplitCore -> "splitcore"
}

# Sanitise a module origin into an object-file stem (`geo.shapes` -> `geo_shapes`).
fn nmod_stem(m: String) : String = nmod_dots(m, 0, string_length(m), "")
fn nmod_dots(s: String, i: Int, n: Int, acc: String) : String =
  if i >= n { acc }
  else {
    let c = string_slice(s, i, 1)
    nmod_dots(s, i + 1, n, cat2(acc, if c == "." { "_" } else { c }))
  }
